      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Because coronary artery disease is the most common cause of death in the United States, much effort is being focused on research into prevention of this killer. Dr. Lush reviews positive and negative aspects of recent trends and summarizes the results of studies on the prophylactic potential of maintenance of normal body weight, exercise, aspirin, fish oils, estrogens, and antioxidants."},
